From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:54:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] Android: keep menus in front when moving between them

Qt for Android stacks its windows as views in the activity. Moving
from one open menu to the next along the menu bar closes the old menu
first, which hands focus back to the main window, and Qt then raises
the main window over the menu that just opened: the menu is open but
out of sight. Raise the open popups again, in the order they opened,
whenever one opens or closes or another window becomes active.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
